RISC-V GCC toolchain (GPL)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The firmware is built with the external `riscv64-unknown-elf` GCC toolchain
(GPL). It is a build dependency only and is NOT redistributed here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Authors / institution
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The chip was designed by the Neuromorphic Edge Computing Systems Lab,
Eindhoven University of Technology (TU/e), by F. Corradi, S. Ye, M. Fattori
and R. Jordans. Author copyright and attribution should be preserved.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cited papers (NOT redistributed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The following articles are cited references only. They are (c) IEEE and are
NOT included in this repository — no manuscript PDF, LaTeX source, or figure
beyond the small attributed image assets under docs/figures/ is shipped.

  * F. Corradi, S. Ye, M. Fattori, R. Jordans, "An Open-Silicon Neuromorphic
    Chemosensing Front-End with Electrode-Pad Wet Transduction," IEEE ISCAS 2026.
  * F. Corradi, S. Ye, M. Fattori, R. Jordans, "A RISC-V-Managed Analog Spiking
    Neural Network Array for On-Sensor Olfactory Processing," IEEE ISCAS 2027.
  * The shared IEEE TBioCAS journal companion panels reuse the same data/scripts.

The README hardware figure (docs/figures/fig_hardware_layout.{pdf,png}) is
composed from image assets of the ISCAS 2026 paper and is reproduced here with
attribution to the authors and (c) IEEE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Metal-oxide odor dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The olfaction experiments use a third-party metal-oxide gas-sensor dataset.
It is cited in the papers; raw third-party features are not redistributed
beyond the derived, paper-facing result files under data/olfaction/.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Large design files available on request
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
To keep the repository under hosting limits, three oversized design files are
intentionally omitted (see docs/HARDWARE_TRAPS.md — "Large files"):
  design/gds/RF_block.gds                                   (~140 MB)
  design/mag/RF_block.mag                                   (~137 MB)
  design/mag/neuron_synapse_array_with_input_output_logic_v2_flat.mag (~104 MB)
They are one-off test structures / flattened layout, not needed to open or
understand the DUT wrapper. Request them from the authors.
